 ::  / MobyDick :: 


 "Meantime, at the first tap of the boat's bottom, the Lakeman had slackened the line, so as to drop astern from the whirlpool; calmly looking on, he thought his own thoughts." [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 

 But, at some distance, Moby Dick rose again, with some tatters of Radney's red woollen shirt, caught in the teeth that had destroyed him. [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 
    "  (refersto) Moby Dick

 '"In good time, the Town-Ho reached her port—a savage, solitary place—where no civilized creature resided.'" [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 

 There, headed by the Lakeman, all but five or six of the foremastmen deliberately deserted among the palms; eventually, as it turned out, seizing a large double war-canoe of the savages, and setting sail for some other harbor. [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 

 But to such unresting vigilance over their dangerous allies was this small band of whites necessitated, both by night and by day, and so extreme was the hard work they underwent, that upon the vessel being ready again for sea, they were in such a weakened condition that the captain durst not put off with them in so heavy a vessel. [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 

 After taking counsel with his officers, he anchored the ship as far off shore as possible; loaded and ran out his two cannon from the bows; stacked his muskets on the poop; and warning the Islanders not to approach the ship at their peril, took one man with him, and setting the sail of his best whale-boat, steered straight before the wind for Tahiti, five hundred miles distant, to procure a reinforcement to his crew. [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 

 He steered away from it; but the savage craft bore down on him; and soon the voice of Steelkilt hailed him to heave to, or he would run him under water. [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 

 With one foot on each prow of the yoked war-canoes, the Lakeman laughed him to scorn; assuring him that if the pistol so much as clicked in the lock, he would bury him in bubbles and foam. [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 

 "‘A pretty scholar,' laughed the Lakeman. ‘Adios, Senor!' and leaping into the sea, he swam back to his comrades." [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 

 '"Watching the boat till it was fairly beached, and drawn up to the roots of the cocoa-nut trees, Steelkilt made sail again, and in due time arrived at Tahiti, his own place of destination.'" [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 

 '"Some ten days after the French ships sailed, the whale-boat arrived, and the captain was forced to enlist some of the more civilized Tahitians, who had been somewhat used to the sea.'" [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 
    "  (refersto) Some French

 Chartering a small native schooner, he returned with them to his vessel; and finding all right there, again resumed his cruisings. [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 

 '"Where Steelkilt now is, gentlemen, none know; but upon the island of Nantucket, the widow of Radney still turns to the sea which refuses to give up its dead; still in dreams sees the awful white whale that destroyed him.'" [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 
    "  (refersto) Where Steelkilt

 "‘Then I entreat you, tell me if to the best of your own convictions, this your story is in substance really true? It is so passing wonderful! Did you get it from an unquestionable source? Bear with me if I seem to press.'" [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 

 "‘Nay,' said Don Sebastian; ‘but I know a worthy priest near by, who will quickly procure one for me. I go for it; but are you well advised? this may grow too serious.'" [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 

 "‘Excuse me for running after you, Don Sebastian; but may I also beg that you will be particular in procuring the largest sized Evangelists you can.'" [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 

 I know it to be true; it happened on this ball; I trod the ship; I knew the crew; I have seen and talked with Steelkilt since the death of Radney. [MobyDick] 
  " (itintab) 54. The Town-Ho's Story. [MobyDick] 

